# Global code quality

## Anti-cheating (mandatory)

- MUST NOT refactor by only moving code without real separation of concerns.
- MUST NOT create modules with artificial separation (for example by line count only).
- MUST NOT implement placeholder logic that returns hardcoded values.
- MUST NOT create fake implementations that skip real business logic.
- MUST NOT use deprecated patterns when a modern alternative is already in the repo.
- MUST NOT create modules that cannot be tested independently.
- MUST NOT skip work due to missing dependencies; fix the dependencies instead.
- MUST NOT use fallbacks that hide real problems.
- MUST NOT create code that can be skipped; code must work or fail clearly.

## Implementation (mandatory)

- MUST implement real business logic, not placeholder functions.
- MUST keep clear separation of concerns when refactoring.
- MUST make code independently testable.
- MUST NOT claim functionality works without implementing it.
- MUST NOT hide problems with silent fallbacks.

## Quality check before claiming done

- [ ] Code performs real business logic (not placeholders)
- [ ] Refactoring creates real separation of concerns
- [ ] Modern patterns match the rest of the repo
- [ ] Code is independently testable
- [ ] Dependencies are fixed (not worked around)
- [ ] Failures are clear and explicit (no silent fallbacks)

